<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n12241" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Cytōrus</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">-ŏs</span></b> ), i,
			m., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Κύτωρος</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a mountain abounding
				in boxwood, and a town upon it, in Paphlagonia</i>, now <i>Kidros</i>, <i><span class="en">Mel. 1, 19,
				8</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Plin. 6, 2, 2, § 5</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Cat. 4,
			13</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Verg. G. 2, 437</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Val. Fl.
				5, 106 al.</span></i>—Hence, </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Cytōrĭăcus</span></b> ,
				a, um, <i>adj., of Cytorus,
			Cytorian</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">de monte,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov. M.
					6, 132</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pecten,</span>”
				i. e. <i>made of boxwood</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					ib. 4, 311</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>III.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Cytōrĭus</span></b> , a,
			um, <i>adj., of Cytorus</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">in jugo,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cat. 4,
					11</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">montes,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					16, 16, 28, § 71</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
